Subject: Fuse a postfix increment whose old value is used

What this does
  Adds `post_inc` and `post_dec`, register opcodes that convert a value to a
  number, keep the result as the expression's value, and write that result
  plus or minus one to a second register. After register allocation, the
  sequence `to_numeric t, x; inc n, t; move_xfer h, n` becomes one
  instruction when `n` has no other reader and no branch target or block
  start falls inside it. Integers and doubles take an inline path; anything
  else runs the same engine conversions as the separate instructions did.

Why we need it
  `a[j++] = v` took three dispatches. The pair counts put `to_numeric -> inc`
  and `inc -> move_xfer` at about 6% of Octane crypto's executed
  instructions and 4-5% of gbemu's.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes, it adds register opcodes; 9999-bc-version-bump covers it.


